---
import AgentPage from '../../components/home/AgentPage.astro';
---
<AgentPage
  name="OpenCode"
  logo="/assets/agents/opencode.svg"
  headline="OpenCode, one per task."
  sub="Ouijit runs OpenCode in a worktree per task, shows when each one is thinking, and teaches it the ouijit command so it can drive the board."
  description="Run OpenCode in parallel with Ouijit: a git worktree and terminal per task, a private server per terminal, live status, and the ouijit CLI in its session context."
  points={[
    [
      'Knows Ouijit',
      'An Ouijit plugin adds the CLI reference to each session, through the session context on OpenCode 2 and config instructions on OpenCode 1, so OpenCode can create tasks, move cards and stage review comments without being told how.',
    ],
    [
      'Live status',
      "The same plugin listens to OpenCode's session events and reports when a turn starts and ends. The card shows thinking or ready.",
    ],
    [
      'A server per terminal',
      "OpenCode 2 normally shares one background server across every terminal. In Ouijit each terminal gets its own, so a session runs in that terminal's sandbox and ends when the terminal closes. opencode -c resumes the newest session of this worktree, not of the whole repository.",
    ],
  ]}
  startHook="opencode"
  faqs={[
    [
      'Do I need to configure anything?',
      'No. Run opencode in any Ouijit terminal. The plugin is pointed at the CLI reference per launch, and utility subcommands such as auth and models pass straight through. Outside Ouijit’s terminals, OpenCode is untouched.',
    ],
    [
      'Which versions?',
      'OpenCode 1 and 2. Status and the CLI reference work on both; the private server per terminal applies to OpenCode 2.',
    ],
  ]}
/>
